{"abstract":[{"text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"title":"Design Principles","role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp"]},{"anchor":"Explanation","title":"Explanation","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux’s surface area looks small — a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol — but the API is opinionated. These principles explain ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"why"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the API has the shape it does, so you can extend it correctly."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"1-State-is-a-value-observation-is-a-class","text":"1. State is a value, observation is a class"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State is a struct. Mutations go through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout State"},{"type":"text","text":", which is predictable, snapshottable, and testable. SwiftUI observation needs an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" reference type. Reconciling these two requires a class that mirrors the struct."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" generates that class for you ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<StructName>Observer"},{"type":"text","text":") and wires up the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance that bridges the two. Don’t hand-write the observer. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pack → reduce → unpack-diff → observe"},{"type":"text","text":" cycle is what gives you per-property re-renders without coupling reducers to a class."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" extends this to nested struct slices: each slice gets its own observer class so observation stays granular even across composition."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"2-Reducers-are-pure-and-synchronous","text":"2. Reducers are pure and synchronous"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers take ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", mutate state in place, and return an optional ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". They never ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", never ","type":"text"},{"code":"throw","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and never call I\/O directly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: pure synchronous mutations are trivially testable, deterministic, and snapshot-friendly. When you need async work (network, disk, timers), return an effect — a "},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" async closure that runs off the MainActor and dispatches follow-up actions back through "},{"code":"send","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"3. Effects run off MainActor; sends hop back","type":"heading","anchor":"3-Effects-run-off-MainActor-sends-hop-back","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable (Send) async -> Void"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":" runs effects in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"type":"text","text":" so they don’t block UI. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor @Sendable (Action) -> Void"},{"type":"text","text":", so dispatching from inside an effect always lands back on MainActor — no manual hops, no race conditions on state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The split is deliberate: effects own the work, the reducer owns the state.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"4. Persistence is invisible","type":"heading","anchor":"4-Persistence-is-invisible","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers mutate ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" properties; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" records every change in a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" debounces and drains those changesets through ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" closures.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You never write "},{"code":"db.save()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a feature. A reducer that adds an item is identical whether the entity is persisted to SwiftData, SQLite, or nowhere — register or don’t register a writer. This is the principle that makes Swidux apps feel small: persistence stops being a concern of feature code.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"5. Synchronous state, async persistence","level":2,"anchor":"5-Synchronous-state-async-persistence","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State updates synchronously inside the reducer for instant UI feedback. Persistence happens asynchronously: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" change tracking is in-memory and free; the debounced persistence flush coalesces rapid mutations into a single batched write.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tap-tap-tap-tap on an increment button updates the UI on every tap and produces one DB write a moment later. Reducers stay synchronous; storage stays cheap.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"6. Plugins are the single extension point","level":2,"anchor":"6-Plugins-are-the-single-extension-point","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything that hangs off the dispatch cycle is a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". Persistence, undo, killswitch, parental gate, paywall — same protocol, same lifecycle hooks. You can add your own without forking Swidux."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two structural patterns:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Core middleware","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":") — action-agnostic. Doesn’t know your action type. Couples only to state shape ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" for undo; "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" keypaths for persistence)."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Domain plugins","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalGatePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", your own) — owns a state slice and an action enum. Wires into your root types via keypath + action lifter + extractor."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The decision rule: "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"does this need to know your action type?","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" If no, write core middleware and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":". If yes, write a domain plugin and use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"7. Bind to the store, not to `@State`","anchor":"7-Bind-to-the-store-not-to-State","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Form inputs read from the store and dispatch on write. Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","isActive":true},{"text":" for the common case (read one property, dispatch one action), and fall back to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Binding(get:set:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the read is a transformation (optional unwraps, derived values) or the setter wraps the dispatch in animation or branching. Don’t buffer mutable form state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and write back on a button.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Why: every mutation flows through the reducer, which means undo\/redo, persistence, and any plugin that watches the dispatch cycle sees every keystroke (subject to coalescing). If you stash state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", those plugins are blind to it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off is more dispatches per keystroke. Coalescing — see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" — collapses bursts of the same action into a single undo step.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"8. Registration order matters at the boundaries","anchor":"8-Registration-order-matters-at-the-boundaries"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" snapshots in "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it must run "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"type":"text","text":" any plugin or reducer mutates state — register it first. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" drains changelogs in "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it wants the post-mutation state — register it after undo. Domain plugins use only "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The recommended order:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. snapshots first","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. drains after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. domain plugins","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)","plugins.register(parentalGatePlugin)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"9-Strict-concurrency-on-purpose","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"9. Strict concurrency, on purpose"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux is built for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swiftLanguageMode(.v6)"},{"type":"text","text":" and assumes Swift 6 strict concurrency throughout. State must be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":". The macros mark generated code carefully. Effects use explicit isolation ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@concurrent"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is friction at first — you’ll get warnings about ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"text":" types. Honour them. The result is a state-management layer that composes safely with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async\/await"},{"text":" and SwiftData without the surprise data races you get from pre-Swift 6 designs.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"10-The-store-is-opinionated-your-app-is-not","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"10. The store is opinionated; your app is not"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux gives you a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol, and three optional plugins. It does not give you:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A dependency-injection container (write your own ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppEnvironment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A navigation library (use SwiftUI navigation)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A network layer (use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":", structured concurrency, or whatever you want)."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An opinion on database (SwiftData, GRDB, SQLite, Core Data — register a ","type":"text"},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and Swidux doesn’t care).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The store owns one job: take an action, produce a new state, run effects. Everything else is yours."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"11. Service shapes: protocol when others implement it, closures when we own it","anchor":"11-Service-shapes-protocol-when-others-implement-it-closures-when-we-own-it","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux services deliberately come in two shapes, chosen by who supplies the implementation:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Protocol"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — when apps or vendor adapters implement the backend:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (RevenueCat, StoreKit, simulated), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(Mixpanel, Amplitude, console), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsService"},{"type":"text","text":" (any JSON host)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A protocol gives conformers a stable, documented contract."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Struct of closures"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — when the library owns the shape and apps only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"configure or mock it: ","type":"text"},{"code":"KillswitchService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ParentalChallengeSource","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SyncPreflightService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Closures make the built-in "},{"code":".live","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":".mock","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"factories and per-test overrides trivial without a conformance ceremony."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The split is a signal, not an accident: if you find yourself conforming to a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"struct-of-closures service, that service was designed to be configured, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replaced."}]},{"text":"Anti-patterns","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Anti-patterns"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"try","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inside a reducer — return an effect instead.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Hand-writing the observer class when you could use ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Calling ","type":"text"},{"code":"db.save()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from inside a reducer — use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Mutating state from inside an effect — effects dispatch actions; the reducer mutates."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Owning the store with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@StateObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"code":"ObservableObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Buffering form state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and committing on submit — bind to the store directly.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Registering "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" before "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — snapshot must precede mutation."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Send":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Send"}],"title":"Send","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Send"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A function for dispatching actions back to the store from within an effect.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/send"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/StateWriter":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StateWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/statewriter","title":"StateWriter","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StateWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Accumulates entity snapshots and produces batched async persistence work.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","title":"SwiduxPlugin","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","title":"PersistencePlugin","abstract":[{"text":"Coalescing persistence plugin.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EntityStore","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/binding(_:sending:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding"},{"text":" that reads a property through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observer tree and dispatches an action when written.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/binding(_:sending:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","title":"binding(_:sending:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"binding"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"KeyPath","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7KeyPathC"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"State"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Observer","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux0A10ObservableP8ObserverQa"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sending","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Binding","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI7BindingV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]}},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","title":"Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","role":"collection","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"UndoPlugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","title":"Effect","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","title":"ChangeSet","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","title":"Plugin Architecture","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingYourFirstApp":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingyourfirstapp","kind":"article","title":"Build Your First Swidux App","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a counter app from scratch and meet the four moving parts of a Swidux project: state, action, reducer, and store."}],"role":"article"}}}